      "content": "that makes sense. so these \"stochastic events\" and random collisions... do they ever do more than just cause a little bit of noise? i mean, if one of these tiny, unpredictable things happens at a really sensitive moment, can it actually act like a little saboteur? \n\nlike, is there a way for these microscopic \"accidents\" to actually target specific parts of the process, almost like they're intentionally trying to gum up the works or steal the resources meant for building muscle? it's hard for me to imagine how something so small and \"random\" could have such a big impact on the whole system.",
